                <article class="bd-article">
                  
  <section id="vera-c-rubin-observatory-data-preview-1-dp1">
<h1>Vera C. Rubin Observatory Data Preview 1 (DP1)<a class="headerlink" href="#vera-c-rubin-observatory-data-preview-1-dp1" title="Link to this heading">#</a></h1>
<p><strong>Release date</strong>: Mon Jun 30 2025</p>
<p><strong>Update</strong>: Tue Jan 8 2026, to correct an <a class="reference internal" href="overview/known_issues_and_subtleties.html#products-wcs-known-issues"><span class="std std-ref">issue with the WCS FITS approximation</span></a>.</p>
<p>Data Preview 1 contains image and catalog products from Rubin Science Pipelines v29 processing of observations obtained with the LSST Commissioning Camera of seven ~1 square degree fields over seven weeks in late 2024.</p>
<p><em>Dataset</em> <em>Citation</em>: <strong>NSF-DOE Vera C. Rubin Observatory</strong> (2025); Legacy Survey of Space and Time Data Preview 1 <a class="reference internal" href="_images/doi.png"><img alt="DOI Logo" src="_images/doi.png" style="width: 15px;" /></a> <a class="reference external" href="https://doi.org/10.71929/rubin/2570308">https://doi.org/10.71929/rubin/2570308</a> [<a class="reference download internal" download="" href="_downloads/ec3d47a16815fe5a9685455206309cc2/dataset.bib"><code class="xref download docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">BibTeX</span></code></a>] to be used when citing the DP1 dataset and this documentation (the link is self-referential).</p>
<p><em>Paper</em> <em>Citation</em>: <strong>NSF-DOE Vera C. Rubin Observatory</strong> (2025); The Vera C. Rubin Observatory Data Preview 1 <a class="reference internal" href="_images/doi.png"><img alt="DOI Logo" src="_images/doi.png" style="width: 15px;" /></a> <a class="reference external" href="https://doi.org/10.3847/1538-3881/ae521f">https://doi.org/10.3847/1538-3881/ae521f</a> [<a class="reference external" href="https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2026AJ....171..360V/exportcitation">BibTeX</a>]</p>
<p><strong>Data Policy:</strong> Only Rubin data rights holders may have an account in the Rubin Science Platform (RSP) and access to Data Preview 1.
All scientists and students in the US and Chile, plus named members of international in-kind teams, have Rubin data rights.
<a class="reference external" href="https://rubinobservatory.org/for-scientists/data-products/data-policy">Learn more about the Rubin data policy</a>.</p>
